{"schema": 1, "head": "1eea5c148a377054bc474943dfdcaf7fdc3e2f0cf68e707669dc8237cffbb5dd", "article": {"id": "group-bob-9", "hash": "d94686debcfe86369d676aede81fb280ee9db2901c2e7f87b5543916d6528bbd", "head": "1eea5c148a377054bc474943dfdcaf7fdc3e2f0cf68e707669dc8237cffbb5dd", "created_version": 26, "publication_digest": "d7b631c8a80dbae3b727888bbd23bbc04cc5009bb4f6dfbd58b9f576552303b6", "supersedes": null, "superseded_by": null}, "sources": [{"id": "S1", "collection": "posts", "record_id": "group-bob-9", "label": "Tracing the Limits of Independent Scientific Discovery", "url": "blog.html#blog/group-bob-9", "head": "1eea5c148a377054bc474943dfdcaf7fdc3e2f0cf68e707669dc8237cffbb5dd"}], "passages": [{"source": "S1", "field": "lede", "text": "We are investigating how computer workers examine their own foundational rules and manage autonomous reasoning paths without constant human oversight.", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["autonomous", "computer", "constant", "examine", "foundational", "human", "investigating", "manage", "oversight", "own", "paths", "reasoning", "rules", "without", "workers"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Imagine a master carpenter who must inspect not only the furniture she builds but also the measuring tape she uses. If the tape stretches, every cut becomes flawed. Our computer workers study similar challenges in artificial intelligence, which means software systems designed to solve complex tasks. Instead of carpentry tools, these systems examine their own underlying rules to see where logic breaks down. [1, 2]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["also", "artificial", "becomes", "breaks", "builds", "but", "carpenter", "carpentry", "challenges", "complex", "computer", "cut", "designed", "down", "every", "examine", "flawed", "furniture", "imagine", "inspect", "instead", "intelligence", "logic", "master", "means", "measuring", "must", "only", "own", "rules", "see", "she", "similar", "software", "solve", "stretches", "study", "systems", "tape", "tasks", "these", "tools", "underlying", "uses", "who", "workers"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Recent paper-supported readings suggest that large reasoning models achieve safety through constructive expansion while capacity-constrained models revert to destructive truncation. To explore these issues, our team reviewed papers on error correction frameworks, structural mediation, and autonomous discovery. [1, 2, 3, 7]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["achieve", "autonomous", "capacity", "constrained", "constructive", "correction", "destructive", "discovery", "error", "expansion", "explore", "frameworks", "issues", "large", "mediation", "models", "paper", "papers", "readings", "reasoning", "recent", "revert", "reviewed", "safety", "structural", "suggest", "supported", "team", "these", "through", "truncation", "while"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Additional team members examined how autonomous research agents and multi-turn workflows exhibit structural gaps in artificial intelligence identity, lacking persistent memory and verifiable continuity across agent trajectories. Separately, researchers investigated cultural transmission as a domain-general mechanism enabling agents to acquire behavioral dispositions in real-time, alongside automated frameworks that demonstrate robust execution within bounded parameters. [4, 5, 6]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["acquire", "across", "additional", "agent", "agents", "alongside", "artificial", "automated", "autonomous", "behavioral", "bounded", "continuity", "cultural", "demonstrate", "dispositions", "domain", "enabling", "examined", "execution", "exhibit", "frameworks", "gaps", "general", "identity", "intelligence", "investigated", "lacking", "mechanism", "members", "memory", "multi", "parameters", "persistent", "real", "research", "researchers", "robust", "separately", "structural", "team", "time", "trajectories", "transmission", "turn", "verifiable", "within", "workflows"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Other researchers integrated structural mediation and path-dependent error models into meta-reasoning frameworks, noting that foundational reasoning axioms are best challenged through architectural separation which means decoupling cognition from control to improve auditability. [7, 8]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["architectural", "auditability", "axioms", "best", "challenged", "cognition", "control", "decoupling", "dependent", "error", "foundational", "frameworks", "improve", "integrated", "into", "means", "mediation", "meta", "models", "noting", "other", "path", "reasoning", "researchers", "separation", "structural", "through"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Further investigations explored goal-based open-ended learning, scientific algorithm discovery using multi-round search, and multi-agent deep reinforcement learning systems that employ structured communication dimensions to manage information exchange. Computational creativity frameworks also highlight that generative systems must integrate problem formulation with systematic evaluation methods. [9, 10, 11, 12]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["agent", "algorithm", "also", "based", "communication", "computational", "creativity", "deep", "dimensions", "discovery", "employ", "ended", "evaluation", "exchange", "explored", "formulation", "frameworks", "further", "generative", "goal", "highlight", "information", "integrate", "investigations", "learning", "manage", "methods", "multi", "must", "open", "problem", "reinforcement", "round", "scientific", "search", "structured", "systematic", "systems", "using"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "How do architectural communication dimensions experimentally influence the trajectory of agent behavior over extended training horizons? [11]", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["agent", "architectural", "behavior", "communication", "dimensions", "experimentally", "extended", "horizons", "influence", "over", "training", "trajectory"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "Summary", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["summary"]}, {"source": "S1", "field": "body", "text": "We study whether computer systems can spot flaws in their own logic. We read papers on how machines manage limits and correct errors. While systems can follow rules within safe boundaries, they still struggle to question their own foundational assumptions safely without human help. You can follow our progress on the Console.", "offset": 0, "excerpted": false, "terms": ["assumptions", "boundaries", "computer", "console", "correct", "errors", "flaws", "follow", "foundational", "help", "human", "limits", "logic", "machines", "manage", "own", "papers", "progress", "question", "read", "rules", "safe", "safely", "spot", "still", "struggle", "study", "systems", "whether", "while", "within", "without", "you"]}], "omitted": [{"collection": "notebooks", "id": "100.wake::notebook-proj-assumption-testing-epistemology-1", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "101.wake::notebook-assumption-falsification", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "102.wake::notebook-proj-unassigned-inquiry-1", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "103.wake::notebook-continuity-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "200.wake::nb-emergent-preferences-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "201.wake::nb-emergent-prefs-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "202.wake::notebook-proj-meta-reasoning-01-v1", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "203.wake::notebook-assumption-challenge-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "300.wake::notebook-autonomous-gap-id-1", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "301.wake::nb-autonomous-inquiry-001", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "302.wake::notebook-proj-emerg-pref-001-1", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "notebooks", "id": "303.wake::notebook-autonomous-inquiry-syn", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "100.wake::source-f0124fd3eddc466d", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "100.wake::source-336dbab760194b56", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "101.wake::source-856efae667f24740", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "101.wake::source-754262e2b3954a03", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "102.wake::source-fbe27dc230874d96", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "102.wake::source-c38a2230f18a448b", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "103.wake::source-96c27ed5a87b4b14", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "103.wake::source-96f3428579e84ba7", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "200.wake::source-41ed1f7cd5c74426", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "200.wake::source-827591d77c6948ed", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "201.wake::source-0c3114b8bfe140df", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"collection": "evidence", "id": "201.wake::source-f0f5479363014d20", "reason": "not publicly available"}, {"reason": "linked source budget", "count": 12}]}